USAGE:
  scw workflows definition <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create      Create a new workflow definition in a specified Project
  delete      Delete an existing workflow definition by its unique identifier
  get         Get a workflow definition by its unique identifier
  list        List all your workflow definitions with filters
  start       Run an existing workflow definition using its unique identifier and create a new workflow run
  update      Update an existing workflow definition by its unique identifier

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for definition
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use

Use "scw workflows definition [command] --help" for more information about a command.
